==============================================================================
SS1  The greedy supports: sample, support-size distribution, and the
     exclusion rule (a control on the object, not on the twin primes)
==============================================================================

  Definition of record.  x = p/q in (0,1), r_0 = x; at step n >= 0 take
  1/(n+2) iff r_n >= 1/(n+2), else skip.  A(x) = {m = n+2 : taken}.
  Exact computation: the least admissible m is ceil(1/r), so the
  support is the greedy Egyptian expansion of x; Fraction arithmetic
  throughout, and the shortcut is cross-checked against the literal
  step-by-step rule below.

