==============================================================================
SS2  Bridge B1: does the greedy support predict the parity class of
     lambda?  The specification's test, and what is left of it
==============================================================================

  THE EXPECTED NULL, STATED FIRST.  A(x) is a deterministic function
  of x alone and carries NO arithmetic input; lambda is multiplicative
  and A(x) is not defined multiplicatively.  There is no a priori
  reason for a signal, so a null result is the expectation; a positive
  result must survive a size-matched control.  A target is ADMISSIBLE
  only if (a) |A| >= 20 and (b) every element of A is small enough to
  factor (here <= 1e13).  By SS1 no target satisfies both.

