SS3  Bridge B2: the rh42 budgets P(p), N(p) are index-parity objects
     (even/odd denominators), not Omega-parity objects
==============================================================================

  P(p) = 2^-p zeta(p)         = sum_{k>=1} (2k)^-p        (even m)
  N(p) = (1-2^-p) zeta(p) - 1 = sum_{k>=2} (2k+1)^-p      (odd m >= 3)
  Both budgets are sums of a function of the DENOMINATOR alone: the
  split they see is the index parity 1_{n even}, nothing else.

  p = 1.5  P = 0.92361416203004019899   N = 0.68876118665544814436
