  WHAT A GREEDY-SINE ATTACK WOULD NEED.  Every object of rh41-rh45 is
  additive in log n (the word depends on sin(2 pi theta), the budgets
  on sum n^{-p}, the balance on sum n^{-it}), while lambda is
  multiplicative and the correlation n -> lambda(n)lambda(n+2) is not
  even multiplicative (SS4).  An attack would need a map from a word
  determined by x alone to positive-density multiplicative information
  about Omega(n) -- and the greedy support is in addition
  Sylvester-sparse (SS1), so it cannot even be tested in the regime
  where such information could live.  That missing map is supplied by
  nothing in this programme.

  HONEST LEDGER.  No progress is claimed on the twin prime conjecture,
  on the parity problem, or on (STAR) sum_{n<=x} lambda(n)lambda(n+2)
  = o(x).  Every number above is a finite check; SS1's Sylvester
  ceiling is the only logically exhaustive statement, and it is a
  statement about the greedy object, not about the primes.

